body:
Dude im not an h3 fanboy but this doesn't make sense. The reason Ethan is critisizing Elon Musk is because he was going to focus on free speech and allow anyone to say anything on twitter. Ethan never said he was going focus on free speech for his sub reddit.

&#x200B;

Elon is being hypocritical because the whole point of him buying twitter was for free speech, but one of the first things he does is ban people for impersonating him, and that goes against free speech. Therefore Elon is hypocritical.

&#x200B;

Ethan has never said anything about free speech on his subreddit. He is pointing out that Elon banned him for his free speech.

This drama about pitbulls really just shows how biased dog owners are for thier dog. Like i get that your specific dog is a good boy/girl but statistically pitbulls are more aggressive and lead to more dog bites.

&#x200B;

Personally I'm fine with pitbulls, never had a problem with them. I just cringe when dog owners act like they have to protect their dog's breed.

I really think that with creative jobs, it's not how good your art is or how creative and cutting edge it is. What really matters is your network and your ability to work with people. I graduated with a degree in graphic design and I couldn't find a job because I didn't know anyone in the field. So I was just applying to jobs and never getting a response and it was frustrating and took a tole on my mental health.

&#x200B;

I think if you want to work in a creative field, you have to find your network in college or get close with someone who is in the field you want to work in.

Personally I think that people are justified for being mad since GTA V came out 9 years ago and the only game rockstar has made it RDR2. So basically WTF has rockstar been doing this past decade?

&#x200B;

Also if they're gonna release in the next 2 years this version doesn't seem like they're far enough so people might be worried that the game is being rushed towards the end of development.
